{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20043",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.5,
      "end_seconds": 2.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Hi, sit anywhere you like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.39,
      "end_seconds": 7.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.94,
      "end_seconds": 14.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.4,
      "end_seconds": 16.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "What's been worrying you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.31,
      "end_seconds": 28.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "I'm here because of trouble sleeping. I just want to get back to normal, uh, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.89,
      "end_seconds": 32.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.45,
      "end_seconds": 35.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "I'd call it mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.48,
      "end_seconds": 43.89,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 43.99,
      "end_seconds": 50.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Ah, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.47,
      "end_seconds": 60.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Erm, I've had tired legs by evening too, for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.09,
      "end_seconds": 64.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.88,
      "end_seconds": 72.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "I'd give it a five, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 74.87,
      "end_seconds": 78.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 80.63,
      "end_seconds": 89.83,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse 68, saturation 98 percent. Temp 37.0 degrees, blood pressure 121 over 79."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.81,
      "end_seconds": 91.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.34,
      "end_seconds": 97.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.39,
      "end_seconds": 100.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.74,
      "end_seconds": 125.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Both calves are soft and not tender, and the pulses at your feet are good."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.19,
      "end_seconds": 142.5,
      "duration_seconds": 11.31,
      "text": "You can sit up now. A few quick ones: swelling of the legs, chest pain, redness of the leg or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.46,
      "end_seconds": 162.19,
      "duration_seconds": 17.73,
      "text": "No, um, no swelling of the legs, no chest pain, no redness of the leg. I did have cramps in my calves at night at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.59,
      "end_seconds": 173.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any back pain or weakness in the legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.3,
      "end_seconds": 178.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Oh, um, nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.14,
      "end_seconds": 182.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Right, your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.83,
      "end_seconds": 183.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.36,
      "end_seconds": 187.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.14,
      "end_seconds": 189.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.72,
      "end_seconds": 192.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_6",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 193.96,
      "end_seconds": 214.74,
      "duration_seconds": 20.78,
      "text": "He is on hydrochlorothiazide, 12.5 milligrams, every morning for my pressure, I give it to him. He is on glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar, I give it to him. It's atorvastatin, at night, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.27,
      "end_seconds": 217.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_6",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 219.2,
      "end_seconds": 226.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "20 milligrams. He is on magnesium tablets, at night, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.32,
      "end_seconds": 230.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.9,
      "end_seconds": 236.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.71,
      "end_seconds": 242.65,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.68,
      "end_seconds": 255.73,
      "duration_seconds": 11.05,
      "text": "I've got diabetes. High cholesterol, for two years. I have depression. I've been reading about it online and it worried me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.6,
      "end_seconds": 269.82,
      "duration_seconds": 11.22,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Yes, high blood pressure and diabetes are known to us, good to have that clear. Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.58,
      "end_seconds": 275.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 275.88,
      "end_seconds": 283.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "I'm not sure that's right. I seem to recall a problem with amoxicillin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.1,
      "end_seconds": 288.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Maybe, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.28,
      "end_seconds": 300.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.01,
      "end_seconds": 304.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Oh, my mother had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.74,
      "end_seconds": 309.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.94,
      "end_seconds": 314.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.47,
      "end_seconds": 318.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.18,
      "end_seconds": 323.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.46,
      "end_seconds": 344.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.96,
      "end_seconds": 349.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "I had my septum straightened in my thirties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.85,
      "end_seconds": 370.28,
      "duration_seconds": 20.43,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This is probably night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. We shouldn't forget a low salt level or low magnesium. Another possibility is a side effect of a medicine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.99,
      "end_seconds": 376.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.74,
      "end_seconds": 395.2,
      "duration_seconds": 16.46,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause do well once it's treated properly. So, to recap quickly. You've had trouble sleeping, mild, and no weakness in the legs or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.01,
      "end_seconds": 399.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Mm, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.53,
      "end_seconds": 411.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for muscle cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.06,
      "end_seconds": 413.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.44,
      "end_seconds": 429.24,
      "duration_seconds": 13.8,
      "text": "We should do a blood sugar test for tingling feet. Keep well hydrated through the day. Let's plan a check in four weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 430.65,
      "end_seconds": 434.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Um, thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 439.68,
      "end_seconds": 441.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}